.TH TENKO-SUSPEND-REPORT 8 "2026-11-10" "Tenko Linux" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
tenko-suspend-report \- collect suspend/resume diagnostics
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tenko-suspend-report
.RI [ output.tar.gz ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tenko-suspend-report
collects the state needed to debug a suspend or resume failure into a tarball:
the kernel PM, ACPI, GPU and input journal messages, the
.B tenko-suspend
cycle lines, suspend statistics, wakeup sources, the Xorg log, dmesg, the
X session and DPMS state, BIOS/EC firmware versions and the pstore crash
archives.
.PP
Run it as root for the complete set.  Without root, dmesg, dmidecode and the
pstore archive are skipped.
.PP
Without an argument the report is written to
.IR /var/tmp/tenko-suspend-report- \fIhost\fR - \fIutc\fR .tar.gz
and mode 0600 is applied because journal excerpts can contain Wi-Fi names.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /run/tenko-suspend
State shared between the sleep hook and the resume probe for the current
cycle.
.TP
.I /etc/tenko/suspend-debug
When present, the next suspend cycle enables the kernel PM debug messages
and the resume probe turns the display back on when it is off.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemd-sleep (8),
.BR logind.conf (5),
.BR journalctl (1)
